==Notes==
*Originally introduced as a "Dragon Hatchling",<ref>[https://archive.md/s5GAU#selection-745.0-750.0 https://archive.md/s5GAU#selection-755.70-755.86]</ref> they were renamed to "Drakes" before release.<ref>https://archive.md/s5GAU#selection-477.0-477.36</ref> Drakes are still referred to in game files as a "Hatchling".
*Drakes have a maximum chase distance of 200 meters from their spawn position. After that, they will drop aggro more easily.
*Players are likely to find Drakes close to a [[Dragon Egg]] protecting it.
*The drops from Drakes are unusually valuable. Their [[Freeze Gland]]s, glowing blue objects dropped on death, are necessary for all frost-based weapons and foods, and their trophy is used to make the helmet for [[Wolf Armor]].
*Appearance-wise, they greatly resemble an [[wikipedia:Amphiptere|Amphiptere]], a winged, legless type of dragon, in stark contrast to Moder who resembles a huge wyvern.
*Drakes may be weak to fire, however, because of the massive damage difference between [[Fire Arrow]]s and [[Obsidian Arrow]]s, Obsidian are stronger (Fire totaling 44 and Obsidian totaling 52)
**This does not make their fire weakness useless, as Fire arrows make a good replacement if you do not have Obsidian arrows yet or just to save materials.

== Lore ==
{{Quote|Let you who read me be aware of the Frost wyrms, one of the most ancient kins sprung from Ymir's body.
The most common form of the wyrm are the Drakes, the small males that cares for the offspring. Most often they can be seen poised by rocky nests guarding the eggs. In contrast, the females are much larger and a rare sight to behold, but once angered they provide a vicious foe.|[[Runestone]]}}

